import Metronome.Glue

/-!
# The elaborated chip-top glue against `Metronome.Glue`

Generated by `lean/glue_check.py` from the Yosys RTLIL of
`{{TOP}}` (SHA-256 of the RTL snapshot: `{{FINGERPRINT}}`).  Every definition
below is the elaborated cone for one register, one output field or one slot of
a vector; every theorem is its equality with the independent specification in
`Metronome/Glue.lean`.  The vector slots are proved one by one so each goal
stays small.

Free per-cycle leaves, by block:

* sources and guards: the unit/line/stream/pointer/host-mailbox outputs and the
  synchronised pin levels (`fl`, `pins_level`, `acc_a`, `acc_r`, `sh_d`, `sh_o`,
  `cn_v`, `lf_s`, `p_dat`, `s_bit`, `s_byte`, `inb`, `sh_done`, `cn_z`,
  `acc_z`, `acc_c`, `acc_n`, `inv`, `outv`, `p_rdy`, `s_end`, `s_mark`, `s_bb`,
  `l_run`, `l_in`, `l_sp`, `l_pina`, `l_pinb`) — each is another block's output;
* the control registers: the host-write strobes (`c_wr_run`, `c_wr_irqen`,
  `c_wr_db`, `c_wr_hin`, `c_wr_hst`), the picked `FLAGS`/`HOST.OUT` words, the
  host data byte, the `HOST.IN` read bus, `frz`, `rst_q` and the sticky/event
  terms — the host-map, move-resolution, data-RAM and queue cuts cover them;
* the output pins: the `cfg` fields (`obind`, `sel`, `lut`, `oe`), the line
  buses (`l_comm`, `l_pina`, `l_pinb`, `l_seg`), `frz` and `rst_q` — the
  latch-bank and line cuts cover their content.
-/

set_option autoImplicit false
set_option exponentiation.threshold 1024
set_option maxHeartbeats 8000000
set_option maxRecDepth 100000
set_option linter.unusedVariables false
set_option linter.unusedSimpArgs false

namespace Metronome.Glue

